%I A400292 #17 Nov 04 2026 17:10:03
%S A400292 1,6,32,32,1620,1620,15900,1879420
%N A400292 Length of the common period length of the smallest n-tuple (for the sup norm) of primes whose reciprocals have the same period length in base 10.
%C A400292 We consider the reciprocals of primes 2 and 5 to have no period in base 10, so they are actually excluded. (If they were considered to have period length 0, then a(2) = 0.)
%C A400292 Other measures of the "size" of the n-tuples, e.g., the taxicab or 1-norm, would give rise to different sequences.
%e A400292 See A400291.
%o A400292 (PARI) apply( {A400292(n)=my(M=Map(),P,s); forprime(p=2,, 10%p||next; mapput(M, P=znorder(Mod(10,p)), if(mapisdefined(M,P,&s), concat(s,p), s=0; [p])); #s<n-1||return(P))}, [1..6])
%Y A400292 Cf. A002329 (periods of reciprocals of integers prime to 10), A084680 (order of 10 modulo n).
%Y A400292 Cf. A400291 (table which lists the actual primes), A400293 (largest prime of the least n-tuple).
%K A400292 nonn,base,more,hard,new
%O A400292 1,2
%A A400292 _M. F. Hasler_, Oct 19 2026
%E A400292 a(8) from _Alper Ferudun_, Oct 20 2026
